{title: Restore Us (Prayer for Unity)}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{genre: Modern Worship}
{style: Ballad}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: D}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}
{license: CC BY 3.0}
{copyright: © 2014 C. Michael Pilato}
{c: © 2014 C. Michael Pilato · Licence: CC BY 3.0 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ · Source: https://github.com/cmpilato/worship-music/tree/main/Restore_Us_Prayer_for_Unity}
{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]When we fracture; [Asus]when we fragment;
[Bm7]When we fall apart.
[D]When forgiveness [Asus]seems so distant
From [Bm7]every [A]injured heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Gmaj7]Even though breath [Gadd2]is flee[Asus]ting —
Even though hearts [Gadd2]may fail —
[Asus]You are our strength [Gadd2]fore[Asus]ver.
Restore [Gmaj7]us.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]In the season [Asus]of disagreement
[Bm7]When we all fall short,
[D]Unify us [Asus]in Christ Jesus
To [Bm7]glori[A]fy our Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
[A]Even though breath [Bm7]is flee[Asus]ting —
Even though hearts [Bm7]may fail —
[Asus]You are our strength [Bm7]fore[Asus]ver.
You restore [Gmaj7]us.
[A]You restore [Gmaj7]us.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Asus]It bears all [Gmaj7]things,
[A]Believes all [Bm]things,
[F#m]And hopes all [Gmaj7]things —
[A]Love endures.
{end_of_bridge}
